    /// <c>*pstr</c> past any consumed bytes before returning.
    /// </para>
    /// <para>
    /// It will not access more than <c>*pslen</c> bytes from the string. <c>*pslen</c> will be adjusted, as well,
    /// subtracting the number of bytes consumed.
    /// </para>
    /// <para>
    /// <c>pslen</c> is allowed to be NULL, in which case the string _must_ be NULL-terminated, as the function will
    /// blindly read until it sees the NULL char.
